Subject: [PATCH] Add seasonal background loader with unlimited image support

Scans the whole seasonalbackground folder on every reroll, so the number of
images a user can drop in is unlimited: there is no cap, no fixed-size array,
and no filename convention.

Memory behaviour is the reason this is safe. Exactly one decoded Image is held
and the outgoing texture is destroyed before the next is decoded, so GPU usage
is one background regardless of whether the folder holds 3 or 3000 files. A
1920x1080 background is roughly 8 MB as RGBA8888 no matter how small the
compressed file is on disk.

Two details of the surrounding code shape this implementation:

- Images are loaded by ABSOLUTE path. ResourceLoader.getFileHandle() tries
  Gdx.files.absolute(file) first and only then walks the registered resource
  locations, so an absolute path resolves without registering the folder as a
  resource location. A relative path would not be found.

- The result is dimension-checked. Image's String constructor catches
  GdxRuntimeException from Pixmap and falls back to a blank 0x0 texture
  instead of throwing, so a corrupt file yields a silently blank background
  unless the dimensions are validated.

Rerolls are event-driven (menu entry, track change) and never per frame, so
the directory listing never runs on the render path.
